{"title":"Career Roadmap · Chemist","role":"Chemist","summary":"A Chemist studies the composition, properties, structure and reactions of substances and applies this knowledge in laboratory analysis, research, manufacturing, quality control and product development.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Chemistry"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Chemist studies the composition, properties, structure and reactions of substances and applies this knowledge in laboratory analysis, research, manufacturing, quality control and product development."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Chemistry graduate, the most realistic initial opportunities are usually in laboratory operations, quality control, analytical testing, chemical testing, production support and junior research roles. More advanced R&D and specialist chemist positions generally become accessible after an M.Sc in Chemistry or a related specialization."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Preparing and analyzing chemical samples"},{"text":"Conducting qualitative and quantitative analysis"},{"text":"Operating laboratory instruments"},{"text":"Performing titration, chromatography and spectroscopy"},{"text":"Testing raw materials and finished products"},{"text":"Maintaining laboratory records"},{"text":"Following chemical safety procedures"},{"text":"Interpreting experimental results"},{"text":"Supporting R&D and formulation activities"},{"text":"Maintaining quality and regulatory documentation"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Sc Chemistry"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"├── Laboratory / QC"},{"text":"│ ├── Lab Technician"},{"text":"│ ├── QC Analyst"},{"text":"│ └── Chemical Analyst"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"├── Industry"},{"text":"│ ├── Production Chemist"},{"text":"│ ├── Process Chemi